        <head>DEPARTURE OF THE HE V. T. B. F. FROM WA RRINGTON.</head>
        <p>DEPARTURE OF THE HE V. T. B. F. FROM WA RRINGTON.</p>
        <p>At the St. Al ban's R.C. Church, on Sunday el ing; the Rector, the Rev. T. B. Feeny, formed his congregation that he was about te the town. The rev, gentleman has been aPr Rector of St. Ann's Priory, E igehill, Liverpool, he informed his hearers from the pulpit, he his sought the post, and is taking it simply by the direr of his superiors. He started his mission work in rington in 1876, whence be came direct from A forth College, and after labouring here for about years, twelve months at St. Mary's and the rest ca time at St. Alban's, he waa removed for five</p>
        <p>- of which he spent in Cumberland, and three in pool. His return was a circumstaoce of much 3 the congregation of Sc. Alban's, and now that laboured with such remarkable success at the inissio' Bewsoy-st. for upwards of four years, his departure_' occasion unqualified regret. Much good and useful has been accomplished under his direction during period. The church has been re-seated, a LadY erected, and finally, during the present vear,the ere of a magnificent high altar and reredos which had proceeding some time became an accomplished The rev, gentleman will take over his new &amp;tie" morrow (Sunday).</p>
